<title>JAPAN: Alberta launches 30 bln yen dual samurai --Nikko.</title>
<headline>Alberta launches 30 bln yen dual samurai --Nikko.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/Australian dollar samurai bond issues were announced by lead-manager Nikko Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p>BORROWER Province of Alberta</p>
<p>    AMT	30 bln yen</p>
<p>    COUPON   5.20%</p>
<p>MATURITY 29 Nov 1999  </p>
<p> TYPE dual samuraiISS PRICEpar   PAY DATE29 Nov 1999</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Nov 21-28</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     AA(S&amp;P), Aa2(Moody's)</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nikko Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Industrial Bank of Japan</p>
<p>NOTE: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive A$5,659.95 for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity. -- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
